.TH ELKS_AOUT 4 "March 2026" "Substrate" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
elks_aout \- ELKS Minix-style 16-bit a.out executable format
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B elks_aout
format is the executable file format used by the Substrate
.B PERS_ELKS
personality.
It follows the Minix-style 16-bit
.B a.out
layout used by ELKS and
.BR elksemu .
.PP
Substrate identifies ELKS executables by the little-endian 32-bit
.I type
field at the start of the header.
Recognized image types are:
.TP
.B 0x04100301
Combined I&D ELKS image
.TP
.B 0x04200301
Split I&D ELKS image
.TP
.B 0x04300301
Historical split ELKS image variant
.PP
The first four bytes of a recognized ELKS executable are therefore:
.IP
\fB01 03 10 04\fR,
\fB01 03 20 04\fR,
or
\fB01 03 30 04\fR.
.PP
Substrate does not treat a standalone
.B 0x0301
or
.B 0x0302
halfword as a sufficient ELKS executable discriminator.
.SH HEADER
The base ELKS executable header contains:
.IP \(bu 2
type
.IP \(bu
header length
.IP \(bu
version
.IP \(bu
text size
.IP \(bu
data size
.IP \(bu
bss size
.IP \(bu
entry point
.IP \(bu
requested heap extension
.IP \(bu
minimum stack
.IP \(bu
symbol-table size
.PP
Substrate also recognizes the relocation and far-text supplemental-header
variants used by ELKS.
.SH EXECUTION MODEL
ELKS programs run as 16-bit protected-mode processes under a private LDT.
The supported ELKS syscall entry vector is
.BR INT\ 0x80 .
.PP
An ELKS process that executes
.BR INT\ 0x20
is treated as attempting a Minix-86 syscall ABI and is rejected through the
kernel's Minix trap path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR execve (2),
.BR signal (2)
